<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομμός</span></b>  (A), ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>striking</i>; esp. <i>beating of the head and breast in
				lamentation</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκοψα κομμὸν Ἄριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					423
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Bion
				1.97
			</span></i> (pl.); hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			in the 
				Att.
			 Drama, <i>dirge, lament</i>, sung alternately by one or
			more of the chief characters and the chorus, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δὲ θρῆνος κοινὸς χοροῦ καὶ ἀπὸ
					σκηνῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1452b24
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
